{title: He Hideth My Soul}
{artist: Fanny J. Crosby / William J. Kirkpatrick}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response, Meditative}
{key: D}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A [D]wonderful Saviour is [G]Jesus my [D]Lord
A [A7]wonderful Saviour to [D]me
He [D]hideth my soul in the [G]cleft of the [D]rock
Where [A7]rivers of pleasure I [D]see
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
He [D]hideth my soul in the [G]cleft of the [D]rock
That [A7]shadows a dry, thirsty [D]land
He [D]hideth my life in the [G]depths of His [D]love
And [A7]covers me there with His [D]hand
And [A7]covers me there with His [D]hand
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
A [D]wonderful Saviour is [G]Jesus my [D]Lord
He [A7]taketh my burden a[D]way
He [D]holdeth me up, and I [G]shall not be [D]moved
He [A7]giveth me strength as my [D]day
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
With [D]numberless blessings each [G]moment He [D]crowns
And [A7]filled with His fullness di[D]vine
I [D]sing in my rapture, "O [G]glory to [D]God
For [A7]such a Redeemer as [D]mine"
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
When [D]clothed in His brightness, trans[G]ported I [D]rise
To [A7]meet Him in clouds of the [D]sky
His [D]perfect salvation, His [G]wonderful [D]love
I'll [A7]shout with the millions on [D]high
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
